\fs48 \cf2 Methods\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 When binding Mojo objects for use from Python, you can expose chosen methods to Python as well, using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/python/bindings/PythonTypeBuilder/#def_method"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb18 \ul PythonTypeBuilder.def_method()}}.\
Currently, Mojo methods being exposed to Python must be written with a modification compared to normal Mojo methods: they must be a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 @staticmethod
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  that takes either 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 py_self: PythonObject
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  or 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 self_ptr: UnsafePointer[Self]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 :\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 python \cf5 import\cf14  PythonObject\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 python\cf5 .\cf14 bindings \cf5 import\cf14  PythonModuleBuilder\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 os \cf5 import\cf14  abort\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 @export\cf14 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 PyInit_mojo_module\cf5 ()\cf14  \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 try:\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 var\cf14  mb \cf5 =\cf14  PythonModuleBuilder\cf5 (\cf22 "mojo_module"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb25         _ \cf5 =\cf14  mb\cf5 .\cf14 add_type\cf5 [\cf14 Person\cf5 ](\cf22 "Person"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25             \cf5 .\cf14 def_method\cf5 [\cf14 Person\cf5 .\cf14 get_name\cf5 ](\cf22 "get_name"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25             \cf5 .\cf14 def_method\cf5 [\cf14 Person\cf5 .\cf14 set_age\cf5 ](\cf22 "set_age"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb15         \cf5 return\cf14  mb\cf5 .\cf14 finalize\cf5 ()\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 except\cf14  e\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         abort\cf5 (\cf22 "error creating Mojo module"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 struct\cf14  \cf20 Person\cf5 (\cf14 Representable\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  name\cf5 :\cf14  String\cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  age\cf5 :\cf14  Int\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb25     \cf5 @staticmethod\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf20 get_name\cf5 (\cf14 py_self\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 )\cf14  raises \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         \cf5 var\cf14  self_ptr \cf5 =\cf14  py_self\cf5 .\cf14 downcast_value_ptr\cf5 [\cf14 Self\cf5 ]()\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         \cf5 return\cf14  self_ptr\cf5 [].\cf14 name\cb1 \
\
\cb25     \cf5 @staticmethod\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf20 set_age\cf5 (\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         self_ptr\cf5 :\cf14  UnsafePointer\cf5 [mut=\cf21 True\cf5 ,\cf14  Self\cf5 ],\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         new_age\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 ,\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25     \cf5 )\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         self_ptr\cf5 [].\cf14 age \cf5 =\cf14  Int\cf5 (\cf14 new_age\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb15     \cf5 fn\cf14  \cf20 __repr__\cf5 (\cf14 self\cf5 )\cf14  \cf5 ->\cf14  String\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf14  String\cf5 (\cf22 "Person("\cf5 ,\cf14  self\cf5 .\cf14 name\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf22 ", "\cf5 ,\cf14  self\cf5 .\cf14 age\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf22 ")"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf16 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Taking 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 py_self: PythonObject
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  allows access to the full 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 PythonObject
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  allocation that a Mojo object instance is stored inside of. Typically though, taking 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 py_self: UnsafePointer[Self]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  will minimize boilerplate in the common case that a method merely needs to access the fields of an object.\
Mojo methods called from Python are currently required to take non-standard self types due to limitations that will be lifted in future versions of Python Mojo bindings.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Static methods\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Python Mojo bindings supports exposing Python 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 @staticmethods
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , bound using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/python/bindings/PythonTypeBuilder/#def_staticmethod"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb18 \ul PythonTypeBuilder.def_staticmethod()}}. A function declared using 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 def_staticmethod()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is callable as a static method on the type within Python, without needing an object instance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 python \cf5 import\cf14  PythonObject\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 python\cf5 .\cf14 bindings \cf5 import\cf14  PythonModuleBuilder\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 os \cf5 import\cf14  abort\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 @export\cf14 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 PyInit_mojo_module\cf5 ()\cf14  \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 try:\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 var\cf14  mb \cf5 =\cf14  PythonModuleBuilder\cf5 (\cf22 "mojo_module"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb25         mb\cf5 .\cf14 add_type\cf5 [\cf14 Person\cf5 ](\cf22 "Person"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25             \cf5 .\cf14 def_staticmethod\cf5 [\cf14 Person\cf5 .\cf14 is_valid_age\cf5 ](\cf22 "is_valid_age"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb15         \cf5 return\cf14  mb\cf5 .\cf14 finalize\cf5 ()\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 except\cf14  e\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         abort\cf5 (\cf22 "error creating Mojo module"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 struct\cf14  \cf20 Person\cf5 (\cf14 Representable\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  name\cf5 :\cf14  String\cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  age\cf5 :\cf14  Int\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb25     \cf5 @staticmethod\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf20 is_valid_age\cf5 (\cf14 age_obj\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 )\cf14  raises \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         \cf5 var\cf14  age \cf5 =\cf14  Int\cf5 (\cf14 age_obj\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb25         \cf5 return\cf14  \cf21 0\cf14  \cf5 <=\cf14  age \cf5 <=\cf14  \cf21 130\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb15     \cf5 fn\cf14  \cf20 __repr__\cf5 (\cf14 self\cf5 )\cf14  \cf5 ->\cf14  String\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf14  String\cf5 (\cf22 "Person("\cf5 ,\cf14  self\cf5 .\cf14 name\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf22 ", "\cf5 ,\cf14  self\cf5 .\cf14 age\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf22 ")"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
