\fs48 \cf2 Keyword arguments\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/functions/#keyword-arguments"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs32 \cf5 \ul Keyword arguments in Mojo}}
\fs32  come in two forms:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Keyword-only arguments: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 def foo(*, x: Int)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  This is not currently supported in Python Mojo bindings.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/manual/functions/#variadic-keyword-arguments"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Variadic keyword arguments}}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 def foo(**kwargs: Int)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  This is supported in Python Mojo bindings when used in the unsugared form: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 def foo(kwargs: OwnedKwargsDict)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . (The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 **kwargs
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  syntax limitation will be removed in the future.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 You can define Mojo functions that accept variadic keyword arguments using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/dict/OwnedKwargsDict/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb18 \ul OwnedKwargsDict[PythonObject]}} as the last argument. A simple example looks like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56333  Python\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 import\cf14  mojo_module\cb1 \
\
\cb15 result \cf5 =\cf14  mojo_module\cf5 .\cf14 sum_kwargs_ints\cf5 (\cf14 a\cf5 =\cf21 10\cf5 ,\cf14  b\cf5 =\cf21 20\cf5 ,\cf14  c\cf5 =\cf21 30\cf5 )\cf14   \cf6 # returns 60\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf16 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 collections \cf5 import\cf14  OwnedKwargsDict\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 sum_kwargs_ints\cf5 (\cf14 kwargs\cf5 :\cf14  OwnedKwargsDict\cf5 [\cf14 PythonObject\cf5 ])\cf14  raises \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  total \cf5 =\cf14  \cf21 0\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 for\cf14  entry \cf5 in\cf14  kwargs\cf5 .\cf14 items\cf5 ():\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         total \cf5 +=\cf14  Int\cf5 (\cf14 entry\cf5 .\cf14 value\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 return\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 (\cf14 total\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf16 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Keyword arguments are also supported following normal positional arguments. Additionally, getting specific keyword arguments is a dictionary lookup on the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 OwnedKwargsDict
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 :\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 collections \cf5 import\cf14  OwnedKwargsDict\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 duration_in_seconds\cf5 (\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     hours_obj\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 ,\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     minutes_obj\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 ,\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     kwargs\cf5 :\cf14  OwnedKwargsDict\cf5 [\cf14 PythonObject\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 )\cf14  raises \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  hours \cf5 =\cf14  Int\cf5 (\cf14 hours_obj\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  minutes \cf5 =\cf14  Int\cf5 (\cf14 minutes_obj\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  seconds \cf5 =\cf14  Int\cf5 (\cf14 kwargs\cf5 [\cf22 "seconds"\cf5 ])\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 return\cf14  hours \cf5 *\cf14  \cf21 3600\cf14  \cf5 +\cf14  minutes \cf5 *\cf14  \cf21 60\cf14  \cf5 +\cf14  seconds\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf16 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In this example, if a call to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 duration_in_seconds()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is missing the required 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb18 "seconds"
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  named argument, a runtime exception will occur:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56333  main.py\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf14  mojo_module \cf5 import\cf14  duration_in_seconds\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb15 # Pass hours and minutes, missing "seconds"\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb15 duration_in_seconds\cf5 (\cf21 4\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf21 5\cf5 )\cf14  \cf6 # ERROR: KeyError\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf16 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Keyword arguments are supported when bindings top-level functions, methods, and static methods.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Variadic arguments\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Python and Mojo variadic arguments are normally written using the following syntax:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 foo\cf5 (*\cf14 args\cf5 :\cf14  Int\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 ...\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf16 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 However, this syntax is not yet supported in Python/Mojo bindings, because functions bound using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/python/bindings/PythonModuleBuilder/#def_function"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb18 \ul def_function()}} support only fixed-arity functions.\
As a workaround, you can expose Mojo functions that accept a variadic number of arguments to Python using the lower-level {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/python/bindings/PythonModuleBuilder/#def_py_function"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb18 \ul def_py_function()}} interface, which leaves it to the user to validate the number of arguments provided:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf14 \cb19 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 @export\cf14 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 PyInit_mojo_module\cf5 ()\cf14  \cf5 ->\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 try:\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 var\cf14  b \cf5 =\cf14  PythonModuleBuilder\cf5 (\cf22 "mojo_module"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         b\cf5 .\cf14 def_py_function\cf5 [\cf14 count_args\cf5 ](\cf22 "count_args"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         b\cf5 .\cf14 def_py_function\cf5 [\cf14 sum_args\cf5 ](\cf22 "sum_args"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         b\cf5 .\cf14 def_py_function\cf5 [\cf14 lookup\cf5 ](\cf22 "lookup"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 count_args\cf5 (\cf14 py_self\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 ,\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 )\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 return\cf14  \cf20 len\cf5 (\cf14 args_tuple\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 sum_args\cf5 (\cf14 py_self\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 ,\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 )\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  total \cf5 =\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 [\cf21 0\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 for\cf14  i \cf5 in\cf14  \cf20 range\cf5 (\cf21 1\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf20 len\cf5 (\cf14 args_tuple\cf5 )):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         total \cf5 +=\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 [\cf14 i\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 return\cf14  total\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf14  \cf20 lookup\cf5 (\cf14 py_self\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 ,\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 :\cf14  PythonObject\cf5 )\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 if\cf14  \cf20 len\cf5 (\cf14 args_tuple\cf5 )\cf14  \cf5 !=\cf14  \cf21 2\cf14  \cf5 and\cf14  \cf20 len\cf5 (\cf14 args_tuple\cf5 )\cf14  \cf5 !=\cf14  \cf21 3\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 raise\cf14  Error\cf5 (\cf22 "lookup() expects 2 or 3 arguments"\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  collection \cf5 =\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 [\cf21 0\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf14  key \cf5 =\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 [\cf21 1\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 try:\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf14  collection\cf5 [\cf14 key\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 except\cf14  e\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 if\cf14  \cf20 len\cf5 (\cf14 args\cf5 )\cf14  \cf5 ==\cf14  \cf21 3\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 return\cf14  args_tuple\cf5 [\cf21 2\cf5 ]\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 else:\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 raise\cf14  e\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

